	I am reporting a bug in the recently posted Tetris version
1.3.  It seems that the high score file gets juked (juked: jewk-ed;
screw up, screw over) when the user's name is eight characters
long.  The high score table is kept in "tetris.h" and is a 15 by 8
character array.  I suggest that Tetris addicts go into the file and
make the array 15 by 15.  It now seems to work fine.

	TETRIS NOTES:

	* I have found a coin-operated video game of Tetris.  Atari
	  put it out last year.  It's not too bad --- if you can 
	  find it.

	* Tetris on our Unix(tm) system has been dubbed "The Game
	  From Hell" due to its addictiveness.  I was in the lab
